  "Question": "The difference between a \\(6.5\\%\\) sales tax and a \\(6\\%\\) sales tax on an item priced at \\(\\$20\\) before tax is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$0.01\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$0.10\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$0.50\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$1\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$10\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Both taxes are calculated from the same \\(\\$20\\) price, so their difference is \\(6.5\\%-6\\%=0.5\\%\\) of that price. Since \\(0.5\\%=0.005\\), the difference is\n\\[\n20\\cdot0.005=0.10.\n\\]\nThus the difference is \\(\\boxed{\\$0.10}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
